<%--
Unauthorized_Error_Page_Component

Displays when a user attempts to access a resource they don't have permission for.
This occurs when authentication succeeds but authorization fails - the user is logged in
but lacks the required permissions for the requested action.

$message - Custom error message (optional, auto-generated if not provided)
$section - Section/resource name being accessed (e.g., "Project", "Admin Area")

The escape link goes to the home of the experience the page belongs to: the portal
dashboard on a portal page, the staff dashboard otherwise (each bundle carries only
its own routes).
--%>
<Define:Unauthorized_Error_Page_Component class="text-center py-5">
    <div class="mb-4">
        <i class="bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-danger" style="font-size: 4rem;"></i>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mb-3">Access Denied</h3>
    <p class="text-muted mb-4">
        <%= this.args.message || 'You do not have permission to perform this action' %>.
    </p>
    <% const _home_url = Rsx_Portal.is_portal() ? Rsx_Portal.Route('Portal_Dashboard_Action') : Rsx.Route('Dashboard_Index_Action'); %>
    <a href="<%= _home_url %>" class="btn btn-primary">
        Go to Dashboard
    </a>
</Define:Unauthorized_Error_Page_Component>
